<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/057Z">Corollary <span data-tag="057Z">11.5.0.15</span>.</a> Let $n$ be an integer and let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $n$-category. Then $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is locally $(n-1)$-truncated as an $\infty $-category. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Combine Proposition <a data-tag="057Y" href="/tag/057Y">4.7.7.20</a> with Example <a data-tag="054Q" href="/tag/054Q">3.5.7.2</a> (or apply Corollary <a data-tag="06RN" href="/tag/06RN">4.7.6.16</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
